Level 1 → 2

Goal: The password is in a file literally named -.

cat - doesn’t work because - is treated as “read from standard input”
cat ./- works because ./ makes it an explicit file path rather than a special character

Password (bandit2): PK8fYLZg2hnHSz83plBL1iEPKdD3QToB

Level 2 → 3

Goal: The file is named --spaces in this filename--.

Spaces split a filename into separate arguments, so each space needs escaping with \ (or wrap the name in quotes)
The leading -- would be read as an option flag, so use -- on its own first to say “no more options after this”
cat -- --spaces\ in\ this\ filename--

